<title>THAILAND: Thai agriculture bank plans 29 bln baht bonds.</title>
<headline>Thai agriculture bank plans 29 bln baht bonds.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thailand's state-owned Bank for Agriculture and Agricultural Cooperatives (BAAC) plans to float domestic bonds worth 29 billion baht during its 1997/1998 (April/March) accounting year, Deputy Finance Minister Chavarat Charnvirakul said on Thursday.</p>
<p>He said the bonds, being issued in tranches starting in April, will raise funds for the bank's lending programme.</p>
</text>
